Subject: [PATCH 5/6] W1-P4: "Login with AYZEN" on all modules (req 7)

OIDC access token (issued to the module's own client) opens a module session via POST /auth/module/oidc, so
sign-in works under MODULE_SESSIONS_MODE=strict. Flows: existing AYZEN user (auto-provision module account +
uid), AYZEN signup (screen_hint=signup), explicit link of an existing module account (credential-verified,
never merged). Per-module rollout flag (allow-list = module client ids), module sign-in screen, migration 127
audit events, dedicated-issuer-aware authorize redirects. Fixes a self-deadlock found by the DB tests.

